# Wave W17-Z (Route 217): gear post — a climbing-gear marker post below the climb face: a snow-capped post with a coiled rope and a piton resting at its foot, where the design’s picks, ropes and pitons sleep along the path under the holds (the climb face itself — climbwall 7 — stands byte-preserved above it, gate data entire). On white turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from Route 216’s drift posts behind it by purpose entire: those mark moving snow, these mark the climbers’ rest.
